  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+9y=0,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(0)={y}^{\u2032}\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{2\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to this boundary value problem in terms of an arbitrary constant $A.$\n\nThe solution is $y=A\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the homogeneous boundary value problem, we first find the general solution and then determine the values of the arbitrary constants that fit the boundary conditions.\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ So, the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x,\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-3A\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x+3B\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n-3A\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\cdot 0)+3B\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\cdot 0)=0\\,\u21d2\\,B=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x).\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{\u2032}\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n-3A\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi )=0,\n$$\n\nwhich is automatically satisfied for any $A.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the BVP is $y=A\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x),$ where $A$ is arbitrary.",
